# complements.tbl — how a complement-taking verb wraps the verb it governs (want to go -> 行きたい is built in; these are the rest)
#   english verb (or a parser-internal key) | japanese template | class of the result
#   template slots are forms of the governed verb:  {dic} dictionary form   {stem} masu-stem   {te} te-form   {ta} ta-form
#                                                   {vol} volitional   {inner} dictionary form, or the negative when the English had "not to V"
#   class: v1 (template ends in る, conjugates as ichidan)  v5  na  fixed (already finite)

like | {dic}のが好き | na
love | {dic}のが好き | na
enjoy | {dic}のが好き | na
hate | {dic}のが嫌い | na
start | {stem}始める | v1
begin | {stem}始める | v1
stop | {dic}のをやめる | v1
finish | {dic}のをやめる | v1
try | {te}みる | v1
keep | {te}いる | v1
forget | {dic}のを忘れる | v1
remember | {dic}のを覚える | v1
decide | {dic}ことにした | fixed
hope | {dic}ことを望む | fixed
need | {dic}必要がある | fixed
plan | {dic}つもり | na
intend | {dic}つもり | na
promise | {dic}と約束する | fixed
learn | {dic}ことを学ぶ | v5
fail | {dic}のに失敗する | v1
continue | {stem}続ける | v1
help | {dic}のを手伝う | v5
expect | {dic}と思う | fixed
seem | {dic}ようだ | fixed
refuse | {inner}ことを断る | v5
agree | {inner}ことに同意する | fixed
manage | 何とか{dic} | fixed
pretend | {inner}ふりをする | fixed
mean | {inner}つもり | na
choose | {inner}ことにする | fixed
prefer | {inner}ほうが好き | na
happen | 偶然{dic} | fixed
tend | {stem}がち | na
afford | {dic}余裕がある | fixed
offer | {vol}と申し出る | fixed
dare | あえて{dic} | fixed
practice | {dic}練習をする | v1
mind | {dic}のを気にする | fixed
be_to | {dic}ことになっている | fixed
give up | {dic}ことを諦める | v1
about_to | {dic}ところ | na
